# NetPilot AI - how Git stores files and how GitHub renders/counts them.
#
# This file changes no source content. Every rule below either pins how a file
# is normalized in the repository (so Linux tooling never sees a stray CR) or
# tells GitHub's Linguist which paths are prose/lab fixtures rather than
# product code, so the repository's Languages bar describes the application.

# --- line endings -------------------------------------------------------------
# The published blobs are already LF, so adding these rules rewrites nothing:
# they keep it that way if a future clone is made with core.autocrlf unset
# (a Linux CI checkout, or another contributor's machine).
#
# Shell scripts must stay LF in the working tree too: bash dies on '#!/bin\r'.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Text that Linux parses: the image build (Dockerfile line continuations) and
# the CI/compose YAML. Normalized to LF in the repo, native on checkout.
Dockerfile text
docker/** text
*.yml text
*.toml text
requirements.txt text
.dockerignore text
.gitignore text
.env.example text
*.py text
*.md text

# --- GitHub language statistics ----------------------------------------------
# Project documentation (phase specs, roadmap, delivery reports) and the README
# are prose deliverables, not code. Marking them documentation keeps the
# Languages bar showing Python/YAML instead of ~50% Markdown.
*.md linguist-documentation
docs/** linguist-documentation

# FRR router configs and captured lab evidence are inputs/outputs of the
# Containerlab lab. The 'daemons' and 'frr.conf' files have no useful extension,
# so Linguist would otherwise guess and skew the statistics.
lab/configs/** linguist-vendored
lab/validation_evidence/** linguist-vendored

# --- diff hygiene -------------------------------------------------------------
# Never show a byte-level diff for binary assets.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
